Package: tolome-base
Architecture: all
Depends: libglib2.0-0t64, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: gdm3, thunderbird, thunderbird-l10n-fr
Description: Base identity of the Tolome system
 Gives the system its Tɔlɔmɛ identity without modifying the files of other
 packages:
  * /usr/lib/os-release is diverted (dpkg-divert) so that base-files can keep
    upgrading while Tɔlɔmɛ names itself (ID=tolome, ID_LIKE=debian);
  * the "vendor-logos" alternative gives the Tɔlɔmɛ logo to the GDM login
    screen and to the vendor emblem, with a higher priority than desktop-base;
  * GRUB uses the distributor name "Tolome" (menu entry and EFI directory);
  * the default user picture (/etc/skel/.face, the Debian swirl of desktop-base)
    is diverted and replaced by the Tɔlɔmɛ baobab; users can still pick their
    own photo in Settings. The baobab is also set as the AccountsService icon
    of ordinary accounts (what the GDM login screen displays), at boot and
    whenever an account is created, without overwriting a chosen picture;
  * the GNOME welcome tour is disabled;
  * Thunderbird replaces Evolution: the dock and the default mail handlers
    point to Thunderbird. evolution-data-server stays for GNOME Calendar and
    Contacts. (The pin of the "gnome" metapackage is part of the image
    configuration, not of this package.)
